<<!DOCTYPE type=`memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki` spec=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/memetic-wikitext`>>

<<^ code=`&#x0001;` from=`?` to=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/filters`>>
<<^ code=`&#x0002;`>>

```toml meta
cacheable = true
role      = "the house's named filters: the law index, course standing, waves and the memory stage as functions any layer may re-seat"
tags      = ["lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/meme"]
title     = "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/filters"
type      = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"
uri-path  = "ha.ka.ba/lares/api/filters"
```

\function lares.law.pins()
[subfilter{$:/config/lares/law/pins}] :intersection[lares.law[]]
\end

\function lares.law()
[subfilter{$:/config/lares/law/pins}] =[prefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/]regexp[^lar:///ha\.ka\.ba/(\w|-)+/api/]!regexp[#]sort[title]] +[unique[]] :filter[regexp[^lar:///ha\.ka\.ba/(\w|-)+/api/]!regexp[#]] :filter[get[$origin-bag]regexp[^lar:///ha\.ka\.ba/bags/(oracle|lares|lararium)$]] :filter[regexp[^lar:///\S+$]]
\end

\function lares.road(state)
[tag[stage/road]] :filter[tags[]removeprefix[road/state/]match<state>]
\end

\function lares.course.citers(pattern,t)
[all[tiddlers]prefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/]!match<t>search:text:literal,casesensitive<t>regexp:text<pattern>] :filter[<currentTiddler>removeprefix<t>prefix[#/]then[no]else[yes]match[yes]]
\end

\function lares.course.text-uncited(t)
[<t>escaperegexp[]addsuffix[(?:\.(?!\w|-)|#/|(?!(?:-|\.|/|#))\W|$)]] :map[lares.course.citers<currentTiddler>,<t>count[]] +[match[0]]
\end

\function lares.course.uncited(t)
[<t>backlinks[]prefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/]!match<t>] :filter[<currentTiddler>removeprefix<t>prefix[#/]then[no]else[yes]match[yes]] +[count[]match[0]] :filter[lares.course.text-uncited<t>]
\end

\function lares.course.standing(t)
[<t>!has[proof]then[open]] :else[<t>get[proof]trim[]is[blank]then[open]] :else[lares.course.uncited<t>then[closed ash-ready]else[closed]enlist-input[]]
\end

\function lares.course(standing)
[tag[stage/course]!regexp[#]] :filter[lares.course.standing<currentTiddler>match<standing>]
\end

\function lares.waves()
[tag[stage/wave]]
\end

These reference titles name the engineer face's instance of the attractor-store title convention, in wake order, as slugs under the reference stage; a later store joins the slug list. The view supplies presence.

\function lares.attractors()
[[discordian-catmas]] [[pattern-integrities]] [[practices]]
+[addprefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/reference/]]
:filter[is[tiddler]]
\end

\function lares.stage(name)
[prefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/]] :filter[<currentTiddler>removeprefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/]removeprefix<name>removeprefix[/]]
\end

\function lares.broken()
[prefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/]lar-refs:out[]prefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/]] :filter[is[missing]]
\end

\function lares.unreached()
[prefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/]!regexp[#]lar-refs:unreached[]]
\end

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! The house's named filters

The house filters stand here as `\function` definitions, defined for every filter the house runs: `[lares.law[]]` (the law index: the pins first, then every canon root meme under a bag's `api/` tree, each row answered from a canon layer), `[lares.law.pins[]]` (the pins that stand as canon law), `[lares.road[state]]` (the road reader until stage road items move; a later change retires it under the canon retirement law), `[lares.course[open]]` (course items whose proof reads blank), `[lares.course[closed]]` (items carrying proof), `[lares.course[ash-ready]]` (proved items without inbound citations), `[lares.waves[]]` (wave titles) and `[lares.stage[state]]` (every title under `lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/<stage>/`, slots too; `[lares.stage[state]!regexp[#]]` keeps the root memes). Citations count only from other memory-stage titles, excluding the item and its slots; literal text matches case and a whole title, with links also checked through backlinks. `lares get filter='[lares.law[]]'`, the wake and the MCP seat's `act(address="lar:///engine.law.indexes")` all run these same functions.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/names`>>

!! Why the names carry a period

TiddlyWiki resolves a user function as a filter operator only where its name holds a period (`filters/unknown.js`); a bare `law` would read as a field name. The `lares.` stem marks the house's own set.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-stack`>>

!! The stack seats it

The daemon reads this carrier's text as the reader's bag stack seats it, TiddlyWiki's own cascade: the topmost layer the reader may read that holds this title answers, a working layer's above canon's, and the functions build from that text. A spirit or an operator re-seats a house function by seating this carrier above (mutability at the root reaches every layer fence); the door's ocap check, its receipts and the base guard still hold for the write that seats it. A house name that fails to parse from the seated carrier (dropped, renamed, in a form no reader takes) reads from the floor the code holds, name by name, and a `lares.` function the carrier adds beyond the house set rides beside them. The functions reach `lares get filter=…`, the MCP seat's `get(filter=…)`, `lares wiki render` and the record port's filter ask from this title alone, never from a `$:/tags/Global` tiddler at another title. A filter naming a `lares.` operator nothing resolves refuses by name.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/operators`>>

!! The operators beside the functions

Two house reads stand as filter operator modules in the wiki VM rather than functions here, since each reads the whole log graph at once: `[lares.heads[]]` answers each stream's heads (an entry no other entry of its stream names as `prev`; `[lares.heads[<pet>#<n>]]` one stream's, two reading a fork) and `[lares.inbox[<pet>#<n>]]` the entries addressed to that instance or its entity that no entry of its stream names directly in `re`. No clock and no `modified` sort decides either. A layer re-seats one by seating a module tiddler at its title (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/tw5/filters/stream`), as it re-seats any module; the msg door (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/engine.msg.lands`) reads the same log law.

<<~/ahu>>

